  {
   "id": 615389,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "John Quincy Adams’s victory in getting the gag rule overturned in December 1844 was, according to him, a victory for all the following except",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1169528,
     "content_html": "the Constitutional right of the people to petition"
    },
    {
     "id": 1169527,
     "content_html": "the ability to stand for the natural human rights of enslaved persons"
    },
    {
     "id": 1169526,
     "content_html": "the preservation of the nation’s highest ideals"
    },
    {
     "id": 1169529,
     "content_html": "the right to send abolitionist material through the U.S. mail"
    }
   ],
